                        "definition": "Percentage share of stationary social welfare institutions which showed at least one type of adaptation for the disabled in the total number of stationary social welfare institutions.",
                      
                        "unit": "percent",
                      
                        "dimensions": "total",
                      
                        "methodology": "Stationary social welfare institution is a facility that provides 24-hour care to people who require it due to age, illness or disability.Stationary social welfare institutions include the following types of facilities:- nursing homes,- family nursing home,- facilities providing round-the-clock care to the disabled, chronically ill or elderly as part of business or statutory activity,- community self-help houses or other support centres for people with mental disorders,- homes for mothers with minor children and pregnant women,- night shelters,- shelters for the homeless.",
                      
